# Front-end coding style (`web/`)

- Early returns; Tailwind only (no ad-hoc CSS tags); prefer semantic tokens from `globals.css`
- Descriptive names; event handlers use `handle` prefix (`handleClick`, `handleKeyDown`)
- Accessibility: labels, `aria-*`, keyboard focus (`tabIndex={0}` when clickable non-buttons), `focus-visible` rings
- Prefer `const` arrow functions; define types when useful
- **No semicolons** in new TS/TSX
- Be concise; no long pre-flight plans unless the user asks
- Leave no TODOs or placeholders for requested work

## Commits (when user asks to commit)

- Format: `<type>[optional scope]: <description>` (imperative, no trailing period)
- Types: `fix`, `feat`, `chore`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, …
- Body explains **what/why**, not implementation detail
